      },
      "body": "<!-- open-swe-review-comment {\"id\":\"f_5202641240\",\"file_path\":\"libs/checkpoint/langgraph/store/base/__init__.py\",\"start_line\":476,\"end_line\":479,\"side\":\"RIGHT\"} -->\n\n🟡 **Non-dict mappings fail in persistent stores**\n\nThis public contract now accepts any `Mapping[str, Any]`, but `put()` forwards the object unchanged in `PutOp`. The SQLite store later calls `orjson.dumps(cast(dict, op.value))`, where `cast` does not convert at runtime, and the Postgres store similarly passes it unchanged to `Jsonb`; serializers reject valid non-`dict` mappings such as `UserDict` or `MappingProxyType`. Consequently code that now type-checks against this signature works with `InMemoryStore` (which explicitly converts with `dict(op.value)`) but raises a serialization `TypeError` with SQLite/Postgres. Please normalize the value to a plain dict for every store path, including directly submitted `PutOp`s, or avoid advertising the broader runtime contract.\n\n*(Refers to lines 476-479)*\n\n---\n*Your feedback helps Open SWE learn. React with 👍 or 👎 to tell us if this review comment was useful.*",
